From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet builds a fillet wider than its face

A fillet whose radius is above the width of the face it sits on (r > 4 on a 4 mm face) has no
start solution in the stripe builder: the contact line on the far face lies outside the face
(#1177).

When Compute() fails for a single straight edge between two planar rectangles at a right
angle, Build now cuts the shape by the prism of the region between the arc and the faces. The
arc stays tangent to the face that lasts and passes through the far edge of the face that runs
out (the pivot), or through both far edges when both run out. The cut must give one valid
closed solid and remove exactly the section area times the edge length; otherwise the failure
stands.

ChFi3d_Builder gains the inline accessor InitialShape(). TKFillet links TKPrim, which it
already reaches through TKBO. Related to #1568.

Upstream: Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT#1668 (fork branch SecondMouseAU/OCCT fix/fillet-wider-than-face). This is the form of that
pull request as it stacks on the earlier patches of this series; where it differs from the pull request
as submitted it is only in the lines the stack made conflict (see Scripts/patches/README.md). The DRAW
test cases under tests/ that the pull request edits are not part of this patch: the build has no Draw.

---
